# Architecture Rules

## Pattern: route → service → repository

- Business logic belongs in **services**, not route handlers.
- Database/persistence logic belongs in **repositories**.
- Route handlers: validate input, call service, return response. Keep them thin.

## Module Boundaries

```
platform/src/
├── ocr/              # Invoice OCR pipeline
│   ├── providers/    # Mistral, Gemini, Claude integrations
│   ├── parser/       # Parsed invoice JSON handling
│   ├── transformer/  # Enrichment, GST, totals, reconciliation
│   ├── pipeline/     # OCR pipeline orchestration, fallback
│   └── repository.ts # Bill persistence
├── shared/           # Types (ParsedInvoiceData), settings, storage, utils
├── analytics/        # Analytics module
├── fraud/            # Fraud detection
├── users/            # User management
├── vendor/           # Vendor management
└── email-intake/     # Email intake processing

web/src/              # React/Vite frontend
└── api/client.ts     # Single HTTP client — all API calls go through here
```

## Persistence

- Firestore + GCS in production; in-memory fallback for `LOCAL_DEV`.
- Never silently change the shape of stored `parsed_data`.

## Critical Contract

- `ParsedInvoiceData` in `platform/src/shared/types.ts` is an immutable contract.
- Never rename, remove, or change field semantics without a dedicated OpenSpec change.
